  "notes": "The songwriter-producer at the centre of modern country's writing rooms. Nearly every parameter here is a deliberate reduction, and the entry states each one as such. Harmony: \"his productions deliberately reduce harmonic event density so the lyric lands: two-bar I–V–vi–IV or I–IV–I–V loops with ii–V turnarounds, no modulation, no chromaticism\" — so only three families carry weight, `halfStepDissonance` sits at zero and `2_bars_per_chord` outweighs everything. Drums: \"a live kit with a programmed clap or snap doubling the snare and a 16th shaker; cross-stick verses; **very low fill density** — the records are groove-static by design so the vocal's conversational rhythm reads.\" Tempo: \"56–120 straight on 2&4, distinctly slow-clustered,\" so the mode sits at 82. The melodic identity is the one thing that is *not* reduced, and it is named: \"melody built from speech — verses at conversational syllable density with minimal pitch movement, choruses on a short repeated cell,\" plus \"lyric-shaped phrase lengths rather than symmetrical 4-bar melodic cells,\" which is why `phraseBars` carries three values rather than the genre's two. ⚠ The light synth sub on the later work sits under a live bass \"mixed forward,\" so no `drums.bass808` block is authored. ⚠ Confidence is medium and the research says why: \"role, roster and the harmonic/rhythmic restraint are documented; per-session technique is not [LOW-CONF].\" ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the snap offsets, the perc density and the counter ratio.",
